{"name":"Exhale","hex":"#d2cec4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"exhale","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To expel air from the lungs through the nose or mouth by action of the diaphragm, to breathe out.","To expel (something, such as tobacco smoke) from the lungs by action of the diaphragm."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An exhalation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/exhale"}],"entries":[{"title":"Exhale (Shoop Shoop)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Exhale (Shoop Shoop)\" is a song by American singer Whitney Houston, featured on the soundtrack for the film Waiting to Exhale. It was released as the lead single from the soundtrack on November 6, 1995, by Arista Records. The song was written and produced by Babyface. A mid-tempo R&B and soul ballad, composed in the key of D-flat major, the song's lyrics speak about growing up and learning to let go. The song garnered mostly positive reviews from critics, many of whom noted Houston's vocal maturity in the song."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/ce/WhitneyHouston_ExhaleEP.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exhale_(Shoop_Shoop)"},{"title":"Exhale (Sabrina Carpenter song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Exhale\" is a song recorded by American singer Sabrina Carpenter from her fourth studio album Singular: Act II (2019), released as the album's second single on May 3, 2019. Before the song's release, Carpenter performed the song as an encore on the Singular Tour."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c1/Sabrina_Carpenter_-_Exhale.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exhale_(Sabrina_Carpenter_song)"},{"title":"Exhalation","blocks":[{"text":"Exhalation is the flow of the breath out of an organism. In animals, it is the movement of air from the lungs out of the airways, to the external environment during breathing.\nThis happens due to elastic properties of the lungs, as well as the internal intercostal muscles which lower the rib cage and decrease thoracic volume. As the thoracic diaphragm relaxes during exhalation it causes the tissue it has depressed to rise superiorly and put pressure on the lungs to expel the air. During forced exhalation, as when blowing out a candle, expiratory muscles including the abdominal muscles and internal intercostal muscles generate abdominal and thoracic pressure, which forces air out of the lungs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Expiration_diagram.svg/330px-Expiration_diagram.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exhalation"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Forest_Whitaker_2014.jpg/500px-Forest_Whitaker_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Forest_Whitaker_2014.jpg/500px-Forest_Whitaker_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Houston personally asked Forest Whitaker (pictured) to direct the video.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AForest_Whitaker_2014.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Whitney_Houston_Milano_2.jpg/500px-Whitney_Houston_Milano_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Whitney_Houston_Milano_2.jpg/500px-Whitney_Houston_Milano_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Whitney Houston performing in Milan during her Nothing but Love World Tour, in 2010","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWhitney_Houston_Milano_2.jpg"}],"sounds":{"exhale":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2b/En-us-exhale.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/2b/En-us-exhale.ogg/En-us-exhale.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Werner's nomenclature of colours greys","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg/500px-Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg","ratio":0.794047619047619,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg","share":0.655625},{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_heron_(00129p).jpg","share":0.63625},{"title":"Kendall's Spavin Cure - Dandy---\"Inform me, sir, why your quadruped should have the audacious effrontery to exhale his obnoxious, reprehensible, odious and offensive breath directly - DPLA - 5a0e89abaf86d7ef2cc141461925b2c0 (page 2)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Kendall%27s_Spavin_Cure_-_Dandy---%22Inform_me%2C_sir%2C_why_your_quadruped_should_have_the_audacious_effrontery_to_exhale_his_obnoxious%2C_reprehensible%2C_odious_and_offensive_breath_directly_-_DPLA_-_5a0e89abaf86d7ef2cc141461925b2c0_%28page_2%29.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg","ratio":0.6316458916306283,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kendall%27s_Spavin_Cure_-_Dandy---%22Inform_me,_sir,_why_your_quadruped_should_have_the_audacious_effrontery_to_exhale_his_obnoxious,_reprehensible,_odious_and_offensive_breath_directly_-_DPLA_-_5a0e89abaf86d7ef2cc141461925b2c0_(page_2).jpg","share":0.26625},{"title":"Exhale (Unsplash)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Exhale_%28Unsplash%29.jpg/500px-Exhale_%28Unsplash%29.jpg","ratio":1.4978723404